#: slug-sync.php:1608
msgid "Content type"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:1617
msgid "This content type nests inside a parent, so plan redirects yourself."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:1618
msgid "WordPress only redirects an old URL by itself for content that does not nest, such as posts and products. It does not do so for pages, whatever tool changes the slug, so import the redirect report into a redirect plugin after applying."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:1619
msgid "A nested URL also contains its parents' slugs. Renaming a parent therefore changes the URL of everything beneath it, and those child URLs are not in the reports, which list only items whose own slug changed. Check what sits under anything you rename."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:1624
msgid "Choose what to do"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:1625
msgid "Start with a preview. Apply uses the same matching rules but saves the proposed slugs."
